From 9b219fb68f98208ba491a7fe22065ba1cac3ca38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew de los Reyes <adlr@rosaiclabs.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:49:58 -0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 2/2] drm/i915/display: Re-enable port sync for tiled
 displays on xe3lpd+

Commit 05cffc074938 ("drm/i915/display: Implement Wa_16024710867")
disabled transcoder port sync from display version 30 onwards. Port sync
is the only thing keeping the tiles of a multi-SST tiled monitor in
vertical lockstep, so without it each tile's pipe starts whenever its own
enable sequence (including link training) finishes. The tiles then
free-run with a constant but random phase offset that changes on every
modeset.

On Panther Lake (display 30.00) with an LG UltraFine 5K (two 2560x2880
DP tiles over Thunderbolt), the right tile is visibly shifted vertically,
measured via PIPEDSL as 362 and 826 lines (of 2962) on two boots. With
port sync allowed again, TRANS_DDI_FUNC_CTL2 on the slave reads 0x12
(enabled, master = transcoder B), the measured offset is 0 (within the
~1 line resolution of back-to-back MMIO reads), and it stays locked
across repeated DPMS off/on cycles and a replug, with no underruns or
other errors.

RFC: the workaround's rationale (Bspec 69965) isn't public, so it is not
clear what it protects against or whether a narrower condition is
possible. As it stands the workaround breaks tiled displays on these
platforms.

Fixes: 05cffc074938 ("drm/i915/display: Implement Wa_16024710867")
Cc: Mitul Golani <mitulkumar.ajitkumar.golani@intel.com>
Cc: Suraj Kandpal <suraj.kandpal@intel.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
index 02a53c984..36b0ecb67 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
@@ -4591,10 +4591,8 @@ intel_ddi_port_sync_transcoders(const struct intel_crtc_state *ref_crtc_state,
 	/*
 	 * We don't enable port sync on BDW due to missing w/as and
 	 * due to not having adjusted the modeset sequence appropriately.
-	 * From, xe3lpd onwards we have defeatured this with reference to
-	 * Wa_16024710867
 	 */
-	if (!IS_DISPLAY_VER(display, 9, 20))
+	if (DISPLAY_VER(display) < 9)
 		return 0;
 
 	if (!intel_crtc_has_type(ref_crtc_state, INTEL_OUTPUT_DP))
-- 
